## 3. PROJECT CONTEXT AND OWNER VISION
`flushed-bot` is a greenfield, single-purpose Discord janitor. Its eventual purpose is to execute manual purges and explicit scheduled sweeps at Discord’s real deletion pace, with cancellation, a machine-parseable audit trail, and a configured per-guild operator gate. The current repository contains documentation only.
Owner Vision Context: Establishing a reproducible Python baseline and a small local quality gate creates a stable foundation for the purge engine port without broadening the product beyond its one job. This PR must make future ephemeral coding-agent sessions able to validate configuration consistently before the engine and Discord integration are added.
Owner-confirmed decisions relevant to this task:
- The first task is project bootstrap; the purge engine is next.
- Python support has a floor of 3.11 and a ceiling below 3.13. Production runs on Python 3.12. No code should depend on behavior introduced after the floor.
- The owner’s purge functionality cog will be supplied for the later engine-port task; it is not required here.
- This task is tooling-only. Package layout and application scaffolding are deliberately deferred.
- There is no existing house test/lint configuration. Establish the smallest compatible local tooling rather than adding a broad toolchain.
